+# Summary
+
+**Changed**
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` handles `"markdown"`, using the project's vendored `tabulate` with `style="pipe"` and `number_format=".2f"`. It then appends a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown`.
+- The vendored `tabulate` was not modified, because its README says changes go through the platform team. It already supports `pipe` style and right-aligns numeric columns by default, so no changes were needed.
+
+**Verified**
+- `python -W error -m unittest` ran 3 tests, all OK, including the exact-output markdown test and the CLI test. `-W error` means no DeprecationWarnings were raised.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` printed the expected table and total (461.93).
+
+**Not verified**
+- I did not render the table in an actual GitHub issue.
+- Cell contents containing `|` are not escaped, because the vendored library doesn't do it. The sample data has no such cells.
